### Now the accent alpha baking
I need `luma(u,v)` from Env_Background. Let me implement:

```csharp
private static float[] artLuma;  // width*height
private static int artW, artH;
private static void LoadArt(Texture2D t) {
    Color32[] px = t.GetPixels32();
    artW = t.width; artH = t.height;
    artLuma = new float[px.Length];
    for (int i=0;i<px.Length;i++) artLuma[i] = (0.299f*px[i].r + 0.587f*px[i].g + 0.114f*px[i].b) / 255f;
}
private static float Luma(float u, float v) {
    int x = Mathf.Clamp((int)(u*(artW-1)+0.5f), 0, artW-1);
    int y = Mathf.Clamp((int)(v*(artH-1)+0.5f), 0, artH-1);
    return artLuma[y*artW + x];
}
```
Note: Color32 index 0 is the bottom-left in Unity (GetPixels32 returns row-major starting at the bottom-left). And v=0 = bottom. So y = v*(H-1). Correct.

Also need the foreground alpha: `fgAlpha(u,v)` similar. But actually for the foreground mesh relief I can use `tForeground.GetPixelBilinear(u,v).a` directly if readable. Simpler: build a downsampled grid once. But GetPixelBilinear per vertex (5.8k verts) is fine performance-wise.

