## Root cause (from the shader math + the two source paintings)

The old builder never really rendered the paintings — it re-built them:

| Symptom | Cause |
|---|---|
| Hard horizontal waterbed seam | `LadyLake_Env_Waterbed` re-drew the painting's lakebed band from a **second** dune mesh with a different tint |
| Flat green upper area | `WaterbedCaustics`, `CausticSheen` and `SunRays` were all full-frame **additive** layers; the additive shader is `Blend One One`, so three stacked lifts flattened the whole water column |
| Repeated jagged stems / UV strips | Kelp meshes sampled **three tiny sub-rects** of `foreground.png` into tall ribbons, green-tinted them, and let `_MainU/_MainV` **scroll** the art inside (I read the shader: `_MainTex` is sampled at `uv + Time*_MainUV`) |
| Broken leaves | `LilyCanopy` cut 3 pad sub-rects into notched discs |
| Stretch/crop | Backdrop authored at x ±2.95 / y ±3.95 = 19 % / 11 % larger than the 497×710 painting |

## The fix

- **One full-frame plate per painting.** `Env_Backdrop` and `Env_Foreground` are relief grids whose mesh UV *is* the painting's own normalised coordinate, so `background.png` and `foreground.png` are reproduced 1:1 and stay registered with the model rig (`P(px,py,z)`). The plate runs 0.4 % past the frustum and **mirrors** its UV outside the 497×710 frame, so the thin cover ring is a seamless continuation of the art, not the clear colour. The duplicate waterbed plate is gone.
- **Accents gated by the art, not by rectangles.** `WaterbedCaustics`/`CausticSheen` are full-frame additive plates whose vertex alpha is baked from `background.png`'s **own luminance** (× a vertical zone) — dark water gets no light, so there is no boundary anywhere to seam and no wash. SunRays became 6 soft-sided ribbons at low alpha.
- **Plants are the painting, not ribbons.** White tint, `_MainU = _MainV = 0` (art can no longer slide), and a generated `Env_SwayMask.png` derived from `foreground.png`'s own alpha so only the stems wave and the pads stay rigid.
- Kept the whole original pipeline (4 DynamicCards shaders, Aeschna textures, `DynamicCardAnimatedMaterialProperty`, 12 s Animator) and every externally-referenced name (`SwordGlow`, `CausticSheen`, `Bubbles`/`Motes`/`Glints`/`WaterbedCaustics` as direct children). Obsolete meshes/materials are deleted at build time. Audio, Integration, Model, Acceptance and the old experiment untouched.

